# Docker build context excludes — see infrastructure/docker/backend/Dockerfile.
#
# The Dockerfile ends with `COPY . .`, so without this file the whole 466MB
# backend directory is sent to the builder and baked into the image. Most of
# that is a *Windows* virtualenv, which is useless in a Linux container and
# would only shadow the site-packages that `pip install` already put there.
#
# Anything excluded here must be either regenerated in the image or supplied
# at runtime. The app needs `app/` and `requirements.txt`; every directory it
# writes to (uploads/, storage/) is created on demand by os.makedirs at boot.

# ─── Secrets ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# .env holds the real Supabase password and S3 keys. Render supplies the
# production values as environment variables, which pydantic-settings reads in
# preference to a file — so a copied .env is pure leak with no upside: it would
# sit readable in an image layer for anyone who can pull it.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ─── Local virtualenv (453MB, built for Windows) ──────────────────────────────
.venv/
venv/
env/

# ─── Python bytecode and tool caches ──────────────────────────────────────────
# `**/` is required: a .dockerignore pattern without it matches only the
# context root, so a bare `__pycache__/` would leave every app/**/__pycache__
# in place — stale Windows-compiled .pyc files shipped into a Linux image.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# ─── Local data that must not become image content ────────────────────────────
# ipreneur.db is the pre-Supabase SQLite database with real project rows. In
# production DATABASE_URL points at Supabase and this file is never read, but
# shipping it puts customer data in the image.
*.db
*.sqlite3
celerybeat-schedule

# Generated decks and uploaded logos from local runs. On Render these live on
# the instance's ephemeral disk and start empty.
storage/
uploads/
*.pptx

# ─── Development scratch: test scripts, run logs, pipeline dumps ──────────────
# Unit tests are not run inside the image; CI runs them from the repo.
test_*.py
_test_step*.py
*_test_output*.json
inline_run.py
run_generate_deck.py
download_playwright_headless.py
crawl_output.json
pipeline_output.json
*.log
*_log.txt
playwright_resolution.txt

# ─── Editor / OS noise ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
